{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1408406-describe-your-freehold","id":1408406,"title":"Describe your Freehold","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-15T13:35:44-07:00","id":1408406,"title":"Describe your Freehold","content":"How would you describe your Freehold?<br /> <br /> Is the community centered around one location? Are there Seasonal Courts or one of the alternatives? Does the Freehold have any rituals or holidays they celebrate?<br /> <br /> When it\u2019s time for a new leader how do they pick them?<br /> <br /> Very curious how people handle their Freeholds differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T14:39:46-07:00","id":1408409,"title":"","content":"Currently the most defining thing about the freehold is that it's rather &quot;British&quot;, the monarchs effectively agree with diplomatic &quot;suggestions&quot;. The main purpose of the Senate is to debate their laws and tweak them to ensure no one is unintentionally made into an oath breaker or conversely an oath breaker can't dance through loopholes or technicalities. As a result the oath(s) of the freehold itself doesn't restrict ones actions directly but simply is an oath to follow the laws of the freehold within its territory. While this has some inherent weaknesses it does ensure that people abroad are not struck by a change in freehold law they were unaware of and one can also review the laws before entering the freehold to ensure any laws that changed won't be broken.<br /> <br /> This has the added benefit of allowing the monarchs to still have the freedom to manage their courts without needing to dedicate everything to running the freehold only to have a shift occur again when the seasons shift. Of course, the monarch is in power and though they allow the Senate to act in their name they have the power to veto any decision the senate proposes. The bargains that enable the seasonal courts would not allow a monarch who was a figure head alone.<br /> <br /> As for the transition of power, it is done as is standard for seasonal courts despite the bizare nature of the senate that serves the interests of both the various courts and the unaligned.<br /> <br /> The courts themselves have carved out their own hollows which is a meeting ground for their court and a bastion if needed. While the freehold has it's own hollow as a meeting place, entrance to the freehold is far more lax than the courts. All one must do is swear to uphold the laws of the freehold while within the freehold in order to gain entry. Though, these hollows are far from homes where changelings stay. They are simply common ground where changelings can meet without worry about outside observers.<br /> <br /> As for the leaders of each court, it truly depends on the court how they select their leader. Some hold elections, others favour the strongest or the cleverest but either way the leaders of each court embody the philosophy of their court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T10:51:45-07:00","id":1450852,"title":"","content":"The Krakenswode, also called the Hall of Mists, the Redsalt Keep and the House on Gull-Cliff, is a Freehold established on the shores of Maine.<br /> <br /> It is a collection of safe houses including an abandoned warehouse and processing plant, the basement of a crusty old bar, in an old art deco theater, a seedy motel, a woman's shelter and part of the city memorial gardens.<br /> <br /> I would describe it as a support group crossed with a guerrilla-style militia organization crossed with a halfway house, with the &quot;royal&quot; elements very faint and subtle. Really no more than echoes of the grandeur it's members recall so painfully.<br /> <br /> The courts are seasonal, rules by:<br /> <br /> -Ave Maria, the Ivory Queen of Spring<br /> -Char, the Shimmering Queen of Summer<br /> -&quot;Cracker&quot; Jack Banson, the Straight-Jacket King of Autumn<br /> -Barrows Walker, the Wight King of Winter<br /> <br /> There are around 50 or so members in all.<br /> <br /> They celebrate the Feast of Flowers, of Fire, of Nightmares and of Ashes as well as the holidays associated with the equinoxes and solstices (they tend to celebrate with an eclectic mishmash of ancient pagan tradition and modern culture's adaptations thereof).<br /> <br /> Thus far, the Crowns have seemingly chosen for themselves. Perhaps due to whatever pact the first changelings made here, the Freehold itself seems to choose the leader of a court, when a chair is suddenly empty.<br /> Other positions are chosen by popular election or are applied for like those within a company, depending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26844-quixote","name":"Quixote","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}